  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat the oven to 220°C/200°C fan-forced. Finely chop the garlic (or use a garlic press). Thinly slice the brown onion. In a medium saucepan, melt the butter with a dash of olive oil over a medium heat. Add the onion and cook until softened, 5 minutes. Add the garlic and cook until fragrant, 1 minute. Add the basmati rice, water, the salt (for the rice) and currants and stir to combine. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 minutes, then remove from the heat and keep covered until the rice is tender and the water is absorbed, 10 minutes.\n• TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam so don't peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-29b12594.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the rice is cooking, cut the cauliflower into small florets. In a medium bowl, combine the tandoori paste, some Greek yoghurt (1 tbs for 2 people / 2 tbs for 4 people), a generous pinch of salt and a drizzle of olive oil. Add the cauliflower and toss to coat. Place the cauliflower on an oven tray lined with baking paper and roast until tender, 20-25 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-3bea21f7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the cauliflower is roasting, roughly chop the cucumber. In a small bowl, combine the cucumber, white wine vinegar, sugar and the salt (for the cucumber). Add enough water to cover the cucumber, then stir to combine. Cover and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-5ec87491.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the cucumber is pickling, pick the mint leaves and thinly slice. Roughly chop the pistachios. Heat a medium frying pan over a medium-high heat, add the pistachios and toast, tossing, until golden, 3-4 minutes. Transfer to a plate and set aside. In a small bowl, combine the remaining Greek yoghurt, 1/2 the mint and a pinch of salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-77a0069e.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When the rice is cooked, add the baby spinach leaves and stir to combine. Season to taste with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-496427d2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain the pickled cucumber. Divide the spinach rice pilaf between bowls and top with the tandoori cauliflower and pickled cucumber. Serve with a dollop of the mint yoghurt. Top with the pistachios and remaining mint.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5eb24f1d9c010c2a4a512dba/step-a8301296.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
